IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa8-helpers`

-- coa8-part15-year.l4: Companies Act 2006, Part 15, Chapter 3 (a company's financial year), ss 390 to 392
-- (lines 4996-5043 of ukpga-2006-46.txt). LAYER 1: the law, objectively.
-- Dates are `Date day month year`. The accounting reference date is a day and month that recurs every calendar year, or "the last day of
-- a month" (which is the 28th or 29th in February), so it is a small type of its own and the calendar year is supplied.

§ `Chapter 3: A company's financial year`

DECLARE `s 391 accounting reference date` IS ONE OF
    `s 391 a fixed day and month`
        HAS `s 391 the day of the month` IS A NUMBER
            `s 391 the month of the fixed day` IS A NUMBER
    `s 391 the last day of a month`
        HAS `s 391 the month whose last day it is` IS A NUMBER

-- ---- s 391: accounting reference periods and accounting reference date ------------------------------------------------------

-- src:5008 | (1) A company's accounting reference periods are determined according to its accounting reference date in each calendar year.
@ref s 391(1) Accounting reference periods are determined according to the accounting reference date in each calendar year (src:5008)
GIVEN ard IS A `s 391 accounting reference date`
      year IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`s 391(1) the accounting reference date in the calendar year` MEANS
    CONSIDER ard
    WHEN `s 391 a fixed day and month` d m THEN Date d m year
    WHEN `s 391 the last day of a month` m THEN Date (`Days in month` m year) m year

-- src:5009 | (2) The accounting reference date of a company incorporated in Great Britain before 1st April 1996 is—
-- src:5010 | (a) the date specified by notice to the registrar in accordance with section 224(2) of the Companies Act 1985 (c. 6) (notice specifying accounting reference date given within nine months of incorporation), or
-- src:5011 | (b) failing such notice—
-- src:5012 | (i) in the case of a company incorporated before 1st April 1990, 31st March, and
-- src:5013 | (ii) in the case of a company incorporated on or after 1st April 1990, the last day of the month in which the anniversary of its incorporation falls.
@ref s 391(2) Accounting reference date of a company incorporated in Great Britain before 1st April 1996 (src:5009-5013)
-- (a) the date specified by notice under section 224(2) of the Companies Act 1985 (given within nine months of incorporation), or
-- (b) failing such notice: 31st March if incorporated before 1st April 1990, otherwise the last day of the month of the anniversary of incorporation.
GIVEN place IS A `Place of registration`
      `the date of incorporation` IS A DATE
      `the date specified by notice to the registrar in accordance with section 224(2) of the Companies Act 1985` IS A MAYBE `s 391 accounting reference date`
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 391 accounting reference date`
`s 391(2) the accounting reference date of a company incorporated in Great Britain before 1st April 1996` MEANS
    CONSIDER place
    WHEN `Northern Ireland` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "incorporated in Great Britain" (subsection (3) is the Northern Ireland rule)
    OTHERWISE
        IF `the date of incorporation` AT LEAST (Date 1 4 1996)
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "before 1st April 1996" (subsection (4) covers later companies)
        ELSE CONSIDER `the date specified by notice to the registrar in accordance with section 224(2) of the Companies Act 1985`
             WHEN JUST ard THEN JUST ard
             WHEN NOTHING THEN
                 IF `the date of incorporation` LESS THAN (Date 1 4 1990)
                 THEN JUST (`s 391 a fixed day and month` 31 3)
                 ELSE JUST (`s 391 the last day of a month` (DATE_MONTH `the date of incorporation`))

-- src:5014 | (3) The accounting reference date of a company incorporated in Northern Ireland before 22nd August 1997 is—
-- src:5015 | (a) the date specified by notice to the registrar in accordance with article 232(2) of the Companies (Northern Ireland) Order 1986 (S.I. 1986/1032 (N.I. 6)) (notice specifying accounting reference date given within nine months of incorporation), or
-- src:5016 | (b) failing such notice—
-- src:5017 | (i) in the case of a company incorporated before the coming into operation of Article 5 of the Companies (Northern Ireland) Order 1990 (S.I. 1990/593 (N.I. 5)), 31st March, and
-- src:5018 | (ii) in the case of a company incorporated after the coming into operation of that Article, the last day of the month in which the anniversary of its incorporation falls.
@ref s 391(3) Accounting reference date of a company incorporated in Northern Ireland before 22nd August 1997 (src:5014-5018)
-- The date on which Article 5 of the Companies (Northern Ireland) Order 1990 came into operation is not in the sources: an input.
GIVEN place IS A `Place of registration`
      `the date of incorporation` IS A DATE
      `the date specified by notice to the registrar in accordance with article 232(2) of the Companies (Northern Ireland) Order 1986` IS A MAYBE `s 391 accounting reference date`
      `the date on which Article 5 of the Companies (Northern Ireland) Order 1990 came into operation` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 391 accounting reference date`
`s 391(3) the accounting reference date of a company incorporated in Northern Ireland before 22nd August 1997` MEANS
    CONSIDER place
    WHEN `Northern Ireland` THEN
        IF `the date of incorporation` AT LEAST (Date 22 8 1997)
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "before 22nd August 1997" (subsection (4) covers later companies)
        ELSE CONSIDER `the date specified by notice to the registrar in accordance with article 232(2) of the Companies (Northern Ireland) Order 1986`
             WHEN JUST ard THEN JUST ard
             WHEN NOTHING THEN
                 IF `the date of incorporation` LESS THAN `the date on which Article 5 of the Companies (Northern Ireland) Order 1990 came into operation`
                 THEN JUST (`s 391 a fixed day and month` 31 3)
                 ELSE IF `the date of incorporation` GREATER THAN `the date on which Article 5 of the Companies (Northern Ireland) Order 1990 came into operation`
                      THEN JUST (`s 391 the last day of a month` (DATE_MONTH `the date of incorporation`))
                      ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text does not say which of "before" and "after" covers the day Article 5 came into operation
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "incorporated in Northern Ireland"

-- src:5019 | (4) The accounting reference date of a company incorporated—
-- src:5020 | (a) in Great Britain on or after 1st April 1996 and before the commencement of this Act,
-- src:5021 | (b) in Northern Ireland on or after 22nd August 1997 and before the commencement of this Act, or
-- src:5022 | (c) after the commencement of this Act,
-- src:5023 | is the last day of the month in which the anniversary of its incorporation falls.
@ref s 391(4) Accounting reference date of a later company: the last day of the month of the anniversary of incorporation (src:5019-5023)
-- (a) Great Britain on or after 1st April 1996, (b) Northern Ireland on or after 22nd August 1997, or (c) after the commencement of this Act.
-- Limbs (a) and (c) together (and (b) and (c)) cover every incorporation on or after those dates, so the commencement date itself is not needed.
GIVEN place IS A `Place of registration`
      `the date of incorporation` IS A DATE
      `the company was incorporated after the commencement of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 391 accounting reference date`
`s 391(4) the accounting reference date of a company incorporated on or after the dates in subsection (4)` MEANS
    IF `the company was incorporated after the commencement of this Act` OR northernIrelandLater OR greatBritainLater
    THEN JUST (`s 391 the last day of a month` (DATE_MONTH `the date of incorporation`))
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in Great Britain on or after 1st April 1996 ... in Northern Ireland on or after 22nd August 1997 ... or after the commencement of this Act"
    WHERE
        northernIrelandLater MEANS place EQUALS `Northern Ireland` AND `the date of incorporation` AT LEAST (Date 22 8 1997)
        greatBritainLater MEANS (NOT (place EQUALS `Northern Ireland`)) AND `the date of incorporation` AT LEAST (Date 1 4 1996)

-- src:5024 | (5) A company's first accounting reference period is the period of more than six months, but not more than 18 months, beginning with the date of its incorporation and ending with its accounting reference date.
@ref s 391(5) The first accounting reference period (src:5024)
-- "more than six months, but not more than 18 months, beginning with the date of its incorporation and ending with its accounting reference date":
-- the end is the first occurrence of the accounting reference date that is more than six months after the date of incorporation (an accounting
-- reference date recurs yearly, so exactly one occurrence lies in a window of twelve months).
GIVEN `the date of incorporation` IS A DATE
      ard IS A `s 391 accounting reference date`
GIVETH A DATE
`s 391(5) the last day of the first accounting reference period` MEANS
    IF inYear AT LEAST bound
    THEN inYear
    ELSE IF inNextYear AT LEAST bound
         THEN inNextYear
         ELSE `s 391(1) the accounting reference date in the calendar year` ard (DATE_YEAR `the date of incorporation` PLUS 2)
    WHERE
        -- the first occurrence of the accounting reference date that makes the period more than six months long, counting the day of incorporation
        -- as the first day: a period of exactly six months ends the day before the six-month anniversary, so a longer one ends on or after it (fork F7)
        bound MEANS `add months` `the date of incorporation` 6
        inYear MEANS `s 391(1) the accounting reference date in the calendar year` ard (DATE_YEAR `the date of incorporation`)
        inNextYear MEANS `s 391(1) the accounting reference date in the calendar year` ard (DATE_YEAR `the date of incorporation` PLUS 1)

-- src:5025 | (6) Its subsequent accounting reference periods are successive periods of twelve months beginning immediately after the end of the previous accounting reference period and ending with its accounting reference date.
@ref s 391(6) Subsequent accounting reference periods (src:5025)
GIVEN `the last day of the previous accounting reference period` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 391(6) the first day of the next accounting reference period` MEANS
    `the last day of the previous accounting reference period` PLUS 1

-- src:5025 | (6) Its subsequent accounting reference periods are successive periods of twelve months beginning immediately after the end of the previous accounting reference period and ending with its accounting reference date.
@ref s 391(6) Subsequent accounting reference periods (src:5025)
GIVEN `the last day of the previous accounting reference period` IS A DATE
      ard IS A `s 391 accounting reference date`
GIVETH A DATE
`s 391(6) the last day of the next accounting reference period` MEANS
    `s 391(1) the accounting reference date in the calendar year` ard (DATE_YEAR `the last day of the previous accounting reference period` PLUS 1)

-- s 391(7) ("This section has effect subject to the provisions of section 392") is a signpost: inert, reason 1 (fork F1).

-- ---- s 392: alteration of accounting reference date ---------------------------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `s 392(1) the periods a new accounting reference date may have effect from` IS ONE OF
    `s 392(1)(a) the current accounting reference period and subsequent periods`
    `s 392(1)(b) the previous accounting reference period and subsequent periods`
    `s 392(1) some other period`

-- src:5028 | (1) A company may by notice given to the registrar specify a new accounting reference date having effect in relation to—
-- src:5029 | (a) the company's current accounting reference period and subsequent periods, or
-- src:5030 | (b) the company's previous accounting reference period and subsequent periods.
@ref s 392(1) A company may by notice specify a new accounting reference date (src:5028-5030)
GIVEN from IS A `s 392(1) the periods a new accounting reference date may have effect from`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 392(1) the company may by notice to the registrar specify a new accounting reference date having effect from` MEANS
    CONSIDER from
    WHEN `s 392(1)(a) the current accounting reference period and subsequent periods` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 392(1)(b) the previous accounting reference period and subsequent periods` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 392(1) some other period` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "having effect in relation to— (a) the company's current accounting reference period and subsequent periods, or (b) the company's previous accounting reference period and subsequent periods"

-- src:5031 | A company's “previous accounting reference period” means the one immediately preceding its current accounting reference period.
@ref s 392(1) "previous accounting reference period" (src:5031)
GIVEN `it is the accounting reference period immediately preceding the company's current accounting reference period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 392(1) the period is the company's previous accounting reference period` MEANS
    IF `it is the accounting reference period immediately preceding the company's current accounting reference period`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company's “previous accounting reference period” means the one immediately preceding its current accounting reference period"

DECLARE `s 392(2) what the notice says about the period` IS ONE OF
    `s 392(2)(a) the period is to be shortened`
    `s 392(2)(b) the period is to be extended`

-- src:5032 | (2) The notice must state whether the current or previous accounting reference period—
-- src:5033 | (a) is to be shortened, so as to come to an end on the first occasion on which the new accounting reference date falls or fell after the beginning of the period, or
-- src:5034 | (b) is to be extended, so as to come to an end on the second occasion on which that date falls or fell after the beginning of the period.
@ref s 392(2) The notice must state whether the period is to be shortened or extended (src:5032-5034)
-- (a) shortened: it ends on the first occasion on which the new date falls or fell after the beginning of the period;
-- (b) extended: it ends on the second occasion on which that date falls or fell after the beginning of the period.
GIVEN `the first day of the period` IS A DATE
      `the new accounting reference date` IS A `s 391 accounting reference date`
      notice IS A `s 392(2) what the notice says about the period`
GIVETH A DATE
`s 392(2) the last day of the shortened or extended period` MEANS
    CONSIDER notice
    WHEN `s 392(2)(a) the period is to be shortened` THEN firstOccasion
    WHEN `s 392(2)(b) the period is to be extended` THEN `s 391(1) the accounting reference date in the calendar year` `the new accounting reference date` (DATE_YEAR firstOccasion PLUS 1)
    WHERE
        firstOccasion MEANS
            IF `s 391(1) the accounting reference date in the calendar year` `the new accounting reference date` (DATE_YEAR `the first day of the period`) GREATER THAN `the first day of the period`
            THEN `s 391(1) the accounting reference date in the calendar year` `the new accounting reference date` (DATE_YEAR `the first day of the period`)
            ELSE `s 391(1) the accounting reference date in the calendar year` `the new accounting reference date` (DATE_YEAR `the first day of the period` PLUS 1)

-- src:5035 | (3) A notice extending a company's current or previous accounting reference period is not effective if given less than five years after the end of an earlier accounting reference period of the company that was extended under this section.
-- src:5036 | This does not apply—
-- src:5037 | (a) to a notice given by a company that is a subsidiary undertaking or parent undertaking of another UK undertaking if the new accounting reference date coincides with that of the other UK undertaking or, where that undertaking is not a company, with the last day of its financial year, or
-- src:5038 | (b) where the company is in administration under Part 2 of the Insolvency Act 1986 (c. 45) or Part 3 of the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989 (S.I. 1989/2405 (N.I. 19)), or
-- src:5039 | (c) where the Secretary of State directs that it should not apply, which he may do with respect to a notice that has been given or that may be given.
@ref s 392(3) A notice extending a period is not effective if given less than five years after an earlier extension (src:5035-5039)
-- The exceptions: (a) a subsidiary or parent undertaking of another UK undertaking whose new date coincides with that undertaking's (or, where it is not
-- a company, with the last day of its financial year); (b) the company is in administration; (c) the Secretary of State directs that the bar does not apply.
GIVEN `the notice extends the company's current or previous accounting reference period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which the notice is given` IS A DATE
      `the end of an earlier accounting reference period of the company that was extended under this section` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `s 1162 the company is a subsidiary undertaking or parent undertaking of another UK undertaking` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the new accounting reference date coincides with that of the other UK undertaking or, where that undertaking is not a company, with the last day of its financial year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is in administration under Part 2 of the Insolvency Act 1986 or Part 3 of the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary of State directs that the bar should not apply` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 392(3) the notice is ineffective because it is given less than five years after an earlier extension` MEANS
    CONSIDER exception
    WHEN JUST excepted THEN
        IF excepted
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This does not apply— (a) to a notice given by a company that is a subsidiary undertaking or parent undertaking of another UK undertaking if the new accounting reference date coincides"
        ELSE JUST bar
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        IF bar
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the company is a subsidiary or parent undertaking (section 1162) is not known, and no other exception applies
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if given less than five years after the end of an earlier accounting reference period of the company that was extended under this section"
    WHERE
        exception MEANS
            `s 362 helper either answer`
                (`s 362 helper both answers` `s 1162 the company is a subsidiary undertaking or parent undertaking of another UK undertaking` (JUST `the new accounting reference date coincides with that of the other UK undertaking or, where that undertaking is not a company, with the last day of its financial year`))
                (JUST (`the company is in administration under Part 2 of the Insolvency Act 1986 or Part 3 of the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989` OR `the Secretary of State directs that the bar should not apply`))
        bar MEANS
            CONSIDER `the end of an earlier accounting reference period of the company that was extended under this section`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
            WHEN JUST earlierEnd THEN `the notice extends the company's current or previous accounting reference period` AND `the date on which the notice is given` LESS THAN `add years` earlierEnd 5

-- src:5040 | (4) A notice under this section may not be given in respect of a previous accounting reference period if the period for filing accounts and reports for the financial year determined by reference to that accounting reference period has already expired.
@ref s 392(4) No notice for a previous period whose filing period has expired (src:5040)
GIVEN `the period for filing accounts and reports for the financial year determined by reference to that accounting reference period has already expired` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 392(4) a notice may be given in respect of the previous accounting reference period` MEANS
    IF `the period for filing accounts and reports for the financial year determined by reference to that accounting reference period has already expired`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A notice under this section may not be given in respect of a previous accounting reference period if the period for filing accounts and reports for the financial year determined by reference to that accounting reference period has already expired"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection only withholds the notice; subsection (1)(b) gives it

-- src:5041 | (5) An accounting reference period may not be extended so as to exceed 18 months and a notice under this section is ineffective if the current or previous accounting reference period as extended in accordance with the notice would exceed that limit.
-- src:5042 | This does not apply where the company is in administration under Part 2 of the Insolvency Act 1986 (c. 45) or Part 3 of the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989 (S.I. 1989/2405 (N.I. 19)).
@ref s 392(5) An accounting reference period may not be extended beyond 18 months (src:5041-5042)
-- "extended so as to exceed 18 months": a period beginning on a day is 18 months long if it ends the day before the day 18 months on.
GIVEN `the first day of the period` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the period as extended in accordance with the notice` IS A DATE
      `the company is in administration under Part 2 of the Insolvency Act 1986 or Part 3 of the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 392(5) the notice is ineffective because the period as extended would exceed 18 months` MEANS
    IF `the company is in administration under Part 2 of the Insolvency Act 1986 or Part 3 of the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This does not apply where the company is in administration under Part 2 of the Insolvency Act 1986"
    ELSE IF `the last day of the period as extended in accordance with the notice` AT LEAST `add months` `the first day of the period` 18
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a notice under this section is ineffective if the current or previous accounting reference period as extended in accordance with the notice would exceed that limit"

-- src:5043 | (6) In this section “UK undertaking” means an undertaking established under the law of any part of the United Kingdom ....
@ref s 392(6) "UK undertaking" (src:5043)
GIVEN `it is an undertaking established under the law of any part of the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 392(6) the undertaking is a UK undertaking` MEANS
    IF `it is an undertaking established under the law of any part of the United Kingdom`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“UK undertaking” means an undertaking established under the law of any part of the United Kingdom"

-- ---- s 390: a company's financial year (it follows s 391 in the file because it uses the accounting reference periods) -----------------

§§ `s 390: a company's financial year`

-- src:4998 | (1) A company's financial year is determined as follows.
-- src:4999 | (2) Its first financial year—
-- src:5000 | (a) begins with the first day of its first accounting reference period, and
@ref s 390(2)(a) The first financial year begins with the first day of the first accounting reference period (src:4998-5000)
GIVEN `the first day of its first accounting reference period` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 390(2)(a) the first day of the first financial year` MEANS
    `the first day of its first accounting reference period`

-- src:5001 | (b) ends with the last day of that period or such other date, not more than seven days before or after the end of that period, as the directors may determine.
@ref s 390(2)(b) The first financial year ends with the last day of the period or a date within seven days of it (src:5001)
GIVEN `the last day of the first accounting reference period` IS A DATE
      `the date the directors determine` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 390(2)(b) the last day of the first financial year` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date the directors determine`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST `the last day of the first accounting reference period`
    WHEN JUST determined THEN
        IF determined AT LEAST `the last day of the first accounting reference period` MINUS 7 AND determined AT MOST `the last day of the first accounting reference period` PLUS 7
        THEN JUST determined
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "such other date, not more than seven days before or after the end of that period, as the directors may determine"

-- src:5002 | (3) Subsequent financial years—
-- src:5003 | (a) begin with the day immediately following the end of the company's previous financial year, and
@ref s 390(3)(a) A subsequent financial year begins with the day after the previous one ends (src:5002-5003)
GIVEN `the last day of the company's previous financial year` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 390(3)(a) the first day of a subsequent financial year` MEANS
    `the last day of the company's previous financial year` PLUS 1

-- src:5004 | (b) end with the last day of its next accounting reference period or such other date, not more than seven days before or after the end of that period, as the directors may determine.
@ref s 390(3)(b) A subsequent financial year ends with the last day of the next accounting reference period or a date within seven days of it (src:5004)
GIVEN `the last day of its next accounting reference period` IS A DATE
      `the date the directors determine` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 390(3)(b) the last day of a subsequent financial year` MEANS
    `s 390(2)(b) the last day of the first financial year` `the last day of its next accounting reference period` `the date the directors determine`

-- src:5005 | (4) In relation to an undertaking that is not a company, references in this Act to its financial year are to any period in respect of which a profit and loss account of the undertaking is required to be made up (by its constitution or by the law under which it is established), whether that period is a year or not.
@ref s 390(4) The financial year of an undertaking that is not a company (src:5005)
GIVEN `a profit and loss account of the undertaking is required to be made up for the period (by its constitution or by the law under which it is established)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 390(4) the period is the financial year of the undertaking that is not a company` MEANS
    IF `a profit and loss account of the undertaking is required to be made up for the period (by its constitution or by the law under which it is established)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "references in this Act to its financial year are to any period in respect of which a profit and loss account of the undertaking is required to be made up"

-- src:5006 | (5) The directors of a parent company must secure that, except where in their opinion there are good reasons against it, the financial year of each of its subsidiary undertakings coincides with the company's own financial year.
@ref s 390(5) The directors of a parent company must secure that subsidiary undertakings' financial years coincide with its own (src:5006)
GIVEN `s 1173(1) the company is a parent company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `in their opinion there are good reasons against it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 390(5) the directors are required to secure that the financial year of each subsidiary undertaking coincides with the company's own` MEANS
    IF `in their opinion there are good reasons against it`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except where in their opinion there are good reasons against it"
    ELSE IF `s 1173(1) the company is a parent company` EQUALS JUST TRUE
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The directors of a parent company"
